From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:26:38 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: resolve dp-port egress numbers from the vendor
 tables

cbm_deq_port, tmu_egress_port, tmu_queue and the egress DMA channel were
each computed by a closed form: dp_port_id + 5, dp_port_id + 15, and
"DMA2TX channel == dp_port_id". Those identities are a coincidence of six
consecutive rows in epg_lookup_table ({6,1}..{11,6}), not a rule, and they
were duplicated across four files, so they could drift apart as well as be
wrong together.

For the WAN port they are wrong, and not harmlessly. dp 15 resolves to
dequeue port 19; dp_port_id + 5 gives 20, and epg_lookup_table's next row
is { 20, CBM_PMAC_NOT_APPL, DP_F_CHECKSUM } - so extrapolating aims WAN
egress at a different functional block rather than at an unused number.
The queue would be 30 instead of 28, and the channel would be picked on
the wrong DMA controller entirely: WAN egress is drained by DMA1TX, not
DMA2TX.

Add cbm_dp_egress_res_get() in cbm_ports.c, next to the epg_lookup_table
it reads, and route all four sites through it. The dequeue port comes out
of epg_lookup_table, which already carries { 19, 15, DP_F_FAST_ETH_WAN }
- the answer has been in the tree, ported and unused, all along. The TMU
queue and DMA binding are not in that table (AVM reads the queue back from
dqm_port_info[].def_qid, which this tree fills only for the DQM-CPU
rows), so they are transcribed from the same vendor source
dqm_port_info is itself filled from: the DQM_DMA rows of cbm_config.c.
Keeping the four numbers in one row is the point - they are one hardware
binding and cannot now be updated apart.

intel_xrx500.c takes a scalar wrapper, cbm_dp_deq_port_get(), rather than
the struct: that TU declares its CQM entry points locally instead of
including cbm.h, and a duplicated struct definition there would silently
stop matching.

LAN invariance was checked rather than assumed: the two tables and both
function bodies were extracted verbatim, compiled against stub types and
run against the closed forms for every dp port 0..15. All four LAN ports
come out bit-identical -- dp 2/3/4/5 -> deq 7/8/9/10, queue 17/18/19/20,
sbid 1/2/3/4, DMA2TX ch 2/3/4/5 -- and dp 15 -> deq 19, queue 28,
sbid 12, DMA1TX ch 15, which is AVM's cbm_config.c row.

The callers' range gates are unchanged, so dp 15 is still rejected
everywhere; this commit only changes where the LAN numbers come from.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
